Appendix B: Glossary of Key Terms

Term Definition
Context‑Quadruple A knowledge representation extending RDF triples with a structured Context field and Source provenance: (Entity₁, Relation, Entity₂, Context, Source).
Endotype A biologically distinct subtype of a disease, defined by a specific molecular mechanism or cellular pathology, enabling stratified treatment.
Hallucination In LLMs, the generation of factually incorrect or unsupported text. In our context, extraction of a false quadruple.
Adversarial Auditing Verification by two independently prompted LLMs that must both agree for a quadruple to be accepted.
Mendelian Randomisation (MR) Causal inference method using genetic variants as instrumental variables to estimate the causal effect of an exposure (e.g., gene expression) on an outcome (PD).
Colocalization Bayesian method to assess whether a GWAS signal and an eQTL/pQTL signal share the same causal variant (PP.H4 > 0.8).
Steiger Directionality Test Statistical test that infers the direction of causality between two correlated variables based on the explanatory power of genetic instruments.
Heterogeneous Graph Transformer (HGT) A GNN architecture that handles multiple node and edge types with type‑specific attention, used here for patient embedding.
Leiden Clustering Community detection algorithm applied to the patient k‑NN graph to identify endotype clusters.
Expected Calibration Error (ECE) Metric that quantifies how well a model’s predicted confidence aligns with its actual accuracy, computed by binning predictions.
Catastrophic Forgetting The tendency of neural networks to lose previously learned knowledge when trained on new data; a major challenge in continual learning.
Elastic Weight Consolidation (EWC) Continual learning method that penalises changes to important parameters. PA‑EWC extends this with prompt‑guided parameter categorisation.
ipTM Interface predicted template modelling score, used to assess the confidence of protein‑protein complex predictions from AlphaFold.
CNS MPO Central Nervous System Multiparameter Optimization score for evaluating drug‑likeness for brain penetration.
hMLO Human midbrain‑like organoid, a 3D cellular model containing dopaminergic neurons and other cell types for in vitro PD research.

