Appendix F: Ontologies and Entity Normalisation

All entities are mapped to the following standard ontologies to ensure semantic interoperability:

· Genes/Proteins: HGNC (gene symbols) with cross‑references to Ensembl and UniProt.
· Diseases: MONDO (Monarch Disease Ontology) for PD and related conditions.
· Cell types: Cell Ontology (CL) for neuron and glial subtypes; custom terms added for newly defined populations (e.g., SOX6⁺ AGTR1⁺ mDA) with provenance.
· Anatomical regions: Uberon for brain regions; spatial coordinates from Visium/MERFISH linked as properties.
· Pathways: Reactome and Gene Ontology (biological process).
· Drugs/Compounds: ChEBI for small molecules, DrugBank IDs for approved/investigational drugs.
· Relations: Biolink Model predicate hierarchy (e.g., biolink:causes, biolink:interacts_with, etc.) extended with custom context‑sensitive predicates.

Entity linking will be performed using a combination of:

· PubTator3 for literature‑derived mentions (genes, diseases, chemicals).
· OGER++ for ontology‑based concept recognition in free text.
· Fuzzy string matching with context disambiguation for ambiguous symbols.

All mappings are stored as reified edges in Neo4j with confidence scores and versioning.

