Appendix G: Experimental Validation Protocol (hMLO) for Top Hypothesis

This protocol is theoretical and designed post‑thesis; it will be fully specified during the PhD.

Hypothesis example: “In SOX6⁺ AGTR1⁺ dopaminergic neurons with GBA1 haploinsufficiency, LRRK2 kinase inhibition reduces α‑synuclein pathology, whereas in wild‑type microglia the same inhibition exacerbates GCase deficit — thus a dual LRRK2 inhibitor + GCase activator combination is required for GBA‑PD endotype.”

Experimental Design:

1. Cell lines: iPSC lines from 3 GBA‑N370S PD patients, 3 LRRK2‑G2019S PD patients, and 3 healthy controls (isogenic corrected lines when available). Differentiate into midbrain organoids (hMLOs) using established protocols (e.g., Jo et al., 2016; Smits et al., 2019) with modifications to enhance microglial incorporation.
2. Treatment arms (day 60–90):
   · Vehicle (DMSO).
   · LRRK2 inhibitor (BIIB122, 100 nM).
   · GCase activator (GT‑02287, 1 μM).
   · Combination (BIIB122 + GT‑02287).
   · Positive control: α‑synuclein preformed fibril (PFF) treatment to exacerbate pathology.
3. Readouts:
   · Primary: Phosphorylated α‑synuclein (pS129) immunofluorescence area per organoid section; mitochondrial membrane potential (TMRM) in TH⁺ neurons.
   · Secondary: Single‑cell RNA‑seq (10x Genomics) on dissociated organoids to assess cell‑type‑specific transcriptional responses, ClpP activity assay, GCase enzymatic activity, cytokine profiling (TNFα, IL‑1β) for microglial activation.
   · Tertiary: Survival of TH⁺ neurons (stereology), lysosomal pH (LysoTracker).
4. Power analysis: Assuming 30% reduction in pS129 with combination treatment vs. vehicle (SD 25%), α=0.05, power=0.8, requires n=12 organoids per group (4 per line). Total organoids = 4 treatments × 3 genotypes × 12 = 144 organoids.
5. Analysis: Mixed‑effects models with random intercept for cell line; differential expression analysis by pseudobulk; interaction terms for genotype × treatment.

This protocol translates the KG‑derived context‑specific hypothesis into a testable in vitro framework, demonstrating the translational potential of the system.

